From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:34:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: msgbuf: never use packet ID 0

brcmfmac hands out packet IDs (the request_id of tx and rx buffer posts)
from a ring of array slots, and slot 0 comes round as soon as the ring
wraps. Broadcom's driver reserves ID 0 as "invalid" and never gives it
to a packet (bcmdhd dhd_msgbuf.c DHD_PKTID_INVALID, and its locker
array, whose slot 0 is never allocated). Firmware written against that
driver may treat a buffer posted with ID 0 as no buffer.

Skip slot 0 when allocating, and reject ID 0 in completions.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
index 664f44607..5928d1507 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
@@ -354,11 +354,12 @@ brcmf_msgbuf_alloc_pktid(struct device *dev,
 
 	*idx = pktids->last_allocated_idx;
 
-	count = 0;
+	/* Packet ID 0 means "no packet" to the firmware: never hand it out. */
+	count = 1;
 	do {
 		(*idx)++;
 		if (*idx == pktids->array_size)
-			*idx = 0;
+			*idx = 1;
 		if (array[*idx].allocated.counter == 0)
 			if (atomic_cmpxchg(&array[*idx].allocated, 0, 1) == 0)
 				break;
@@ -388,7 +389,7 @@ brcmf_msgbuf_get_pktid(struct device *dev, struct brcmf_msgbuf_pktids *pktids,
 	struct brcmf_msgbuf_pktid *pktid;
 	struct sk_buff *skb;
 
-	if (idx >= pktids->array_size) {
+	if (idx == 0 || idx >= pktids->array_size) {
 		brcmf_err("Invalid packet id %d (max %d)\n", idx,
 			  pktids->array_size);
 		return NULL;
